---

Warli Painting is an ancient tribal art form that shows tribal cultural practices. I was enamoured by the simplicity and directness of the communication. It represents a communal social scene. In my view, this connects the dying past to the exploding present.

As a next phase, I will try to implement modern cultural scenes using Warli art as a way to critique the evolving social systems that used to protect an individual. What if Warli Painting were to be drawn today?
